# NOTE: this file is itself TRACKED (D-001). It previously contained the line
# `.gitignore`, which made it ignore itself — so it never reached a clean clone,
# and neither did any of the protections below.

# Real participant data NEVER enters this repository (DESIGN.md §8).
data/

# Generated analysis outputs. Report *sources* are tracked; rendered artifacts are not.
reports/**
!reports/**/
!reports/**/*.Rmd
!reports/**/*.qmd
!reports/**/*.md
!reports/.gitkeep

# Anything that could carry controlled-tier content out of the Workbench.
# The R -> Python contract file (D-005) is DATA, not code: it never gets committed.
*.parquet
*.feather
phenotypes_v*.csv
*_phenotypes*.csv
*_phenotypes_formatted*.csv

# Credentials.
*.pem
*.key
service-account*.json
.env
.Renviron
fixture/build/queries/secret.txt

# The fixture's regenerable DuckDB binary is ignored by fixture/.gitignore, not here.
# fixture/bucket/ IS tracked on purpose: it is synthetic, and it is the offline test substrate.

# Tooling noise
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.venv/
venv/
.Rhistory
.RData
# testthat writes a reproduction script per failure here; scratch, not source.
tests/testthat/_problems/
.Rproj.user/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Markdown is LOCAL-ONLY as of 2026-08-31 (user decision).
#
# The repository on GitHub now carries only what has to run inside the All of Us Workbench: R under
# src/, SQL under sql/, configs/, tests/, and the offline fixture. Every .md file -- the design notes,
# the decision log, the runbooks, CLAUDE.md, README.md -- still exists on disk and in git HISTORY
# (`git log --all -- DESIGN.md`), it is simply no longer tracked, so it does not travel to GitHub or
# into a Workbench clone.
#
# CONSEQUENCE, and it is the one that bites: a `git pull` in the Workbench will NOT bring any
# documentation with it. Every instruction needed to RUN something therefore has to live in the header
# of the R file that does it. src/workbench/*.R are written that way on purpose -- if you add a script,
# put its run instructions in the file, not in a runbook nobody will receive.
#
# To put a file back: `git add -f <file>`.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.md
